Go.dot patch 0001 for JUCE, a change of Go.dot's own: a touch source may exist on macOS.

macOS treats a USB touch screen as a mouse and never sends an application touch
events. Go.dot reads the panel itself, through spatcore's MacHidTouchManager
(controllers/touch/macos), which switches the panel out of mouse emulation and
hands each finger to JUCE as a touch source of its own through
ComponentPeer::handleMouseEvent with a touchIndex - so the desk, the cart's pads,
the send and fade mixers and the Stream Deck picture take several fingers at once
(namespace draft section 125, the author's decision BFD of 2026-10-31). JUCE
answers MouseInputSourceList::canUseTouch() false on the Mac, and every injected
finger is then dropped without a word. This answers true. AppKit itself never
sends a touch event, so nothing else changes. It is spatcore's patches/juce/macos
patch, which WFS-DIY carries the same way, with Go.dot's notice in place of
WFS-DIY's.

Not JUCE's own fix, which is why it is not in patches/JUCE: that series is for
fixes JUCE has made. Applied on every platform so every build tree has one state;
the file compiles on macOS alone. tests/ToolchainTests.cpp reads the notice on
every platform and, on a Mac, asks JUCE for a second touch source. The hunk
carries a notice that Go.dot modified the file (AGPL-3 and GPL-3, section 5(a)).

LINE ENDINGS. JUCE stores this file with CRLF, so the hunk's lines end in CRLF and
must stay so; .gitattributes keeps this file byte for byte (-text).

Applied by Go.dot's build, cmake/WfgJucePatches.cmake, in the order
patches/JUCE-local/series gives; refreshed from the working tree with
scripts/patches.py JUCE-local refresh, which keeps this header. Against JUCE
37c894f83d37 (8.0.13+7, the JUCE Tracktion Engine 13b5132 pins). Drop it when JUCE
lets a touch source exist on macOS, or when the panel reader no longer injects.

